  "summary": "Florid Iranian court painting of the Qajar era: jewelled oil portraits, lacquerwork and illustrated books.",
  "description": "Under the Qajar shahs, Iranian painting absorbed European oil technique while keeping Persian profile conventions: monumental portraits of Fath-Ali Shah with enormous black beard, jewelled crowns and brocaded robes; flattened figures set against spray-filled grounds; lacquer pen boxes and mirror cases painted with flowers and single figures. Mihr 'Ali's imperial portraits, Sani al-Mulk's illustrated One Thousand and One Nights and Kamal al-Molk's naturalistic turn mark its arc from court spectacle to academic realism.",
